From: Etienne Lachance <estheban@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:30:00 -0500
Subject: Fix GHSA-f6gg-rchx-xw8j: mixed case HTTPS and FTPS

Backport of php/php-src@9c0b44ffd663 (CVE-2026-128064) to PHP 5.6.

The http:// and ftp:// stream wrappers matched URL schemes
case-insensitively, but only enabled TLS when the character at a fixed
position was a lowercase 's'. HTTPS://, httpS:// and FTPS:// URLs,
including redirect targets, were sent in cleartext. Compare the whole
scheme case-insensitively instead.

The upstream phpt tests are not backported: they rely on
ServerClientTestCase features that PHP 5.6 does not have.
---
 ext/standard/ftp_fopen_wrapper.c  | 2 +-
 ext/standard/http_fopen_wrapper.c | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/ext/standard/ftp_fopen_wrapper.c
+++ b/ext/standard/ftp_fopen_wrapper.c
@@ -150,7 +150,7 @@
 		return NULL;
 	}
 
-	use_ssl = resource->scheme && (strlen(resource->scheme) > 3) && resource->scheme[3] == 's';
+	use_ssl = resource->scheme && strcasecmp(resource->scheme, "ftps") == 0;
 
 	/* use port 21 if one wasn't specified */
 	if (resource->port == 0)
--- a/ext/standard/http_fopen_wrapper.c
+++ b/ext/standard/http_fopen_wrapper.c
@@ -188,7 +188,7 @@
 			zval_dtor(&ztmp);
 		}
 
-		use_ssl = resource->scheme && (strlen(resource->scheme) > 4) && resource->scheme[4] == 's';
+		use_ssl = resource->scheme && strcasecmp(resource->scheme, "https") == 0;
 		/* choose default ports */
 		if (use_ssl && resource->port == 0)
 			resource->port = 443;
